{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Is the Data You Collect Adding Value?"}, {"type": "position", "content": 4}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when talking about collecting data. "}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe ways of solving problems and getting things done in written and spoken situations and in work and social contexts. Train the system users on application structuring and management, according to the established plan and user profile, according to the organization policies."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.  Exchanges information on managing a proposed application, using available hardware for an application, and technical reports on an IT solution."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n8le01ob04re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Modal Verbs to Talk Hypothetically about the Past (Would have, Should have, and Could have)"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "We can use <span class=\"strong\">modal verbs like could, should</span> or <span class=\"strong\">would</span> when we want to talk about a possible event that could happened in the past but did not. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "   The structure of the modal verbs used to talk hypothetically about the past is the following:</br></br>   <span class=\"strong\">Affirmative</span>: Modal verb + have + past participle of the main verb.</br>  <span class=\"strong\">Negative</span>: Modal verb + not + have + past participle of the main verb.</br></br>  Example:</br>  <span class=\"italic\">We <span class=\"strong\">should have collected</span> only the necessary data.</span></br> <span class=\"italic\">We <span class=\"strong\">should not have collected </span>so much data.</span></br></br>   Let's take a look at the meaning of the different modal verbs.</br></br>   <div class=\"center_text\"><span class=\"strong\">Could</span></div></br></br>  <span class=\"strong\">Affirmative</span>: It is used to talk about something that was likely to happen but did not.</br></br>  Example:</br> <span class=\"italic\">The <span class=\"strong\">defects could have been </span>better addressed, with the appropriate data.</span></br></br>  <span class=\"strong\">Negative</span>: It is used to talk about something that was not possible to happen in the past.</br></br>  Example: </br> <span class=\"italic\">The <span class=\"strong\">defects could not have been detected</span>, even with the appropriate data.</span></br></br>  <div class=\"center_text\"><span class=\"strong\">Should</span></div></br></br>  <span class=\"strong\">Affirmative</span>: It is used to express that the ideal was for something to happen, but it did not. </br></br>  Example: </br> <span class=\"italic\">We should<span class=\"strong\"> have tracked</span> the defects from the beginning. </span></br></br>  <span class=\"strong\">Negative</span>: It is used to express that the ideal was for something not to happen.</br></br>  Example: </br> <span class=\"italic\">We <span class=\"strong\">should not have tracked</span> the defects from the beginning.</span></br></br>  <div class=\"center_text\"><span class=\"strong\">Would</span></div></br></br>  <span class=\"strong\">Affirmative</span>: It is either used to express something you wanted to happen but did not or as part of the main clause in the third conditional. </br></br>  Example: </br> <span class=\"italic\">Too bad we did not know about CMMI before, <span class=\"strong\">we would have improved</span> the performance of the process areas.</span> </br> <span class=\"italic\">If we had taken into consideration the importance of the processes needed to develop software,<span class=\"strong\"> we would have been</span> much more effective and obtained a higher quality product.</span></br></br>  <span class=\"strong\">Negative</span>: It is used to express a choice someone was unlikely to have taken.</br></br>  Example: </br> <span class=\"italic\">We <span class=\"strong\">would not have improved</span> the performance of the process areas.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Collecting data for defect tracking is pivotal for our company, since we wouldn't have been able to fix so many defects if it weren't for this process. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "We shouldn't have thought that by entering as much data as possible we were going to improve the defect tracking process. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "This process could have been less tedious, but we weren't selective with the data we collected. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "What is CMMI?"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "CMMI stands for Capability Maturity Model Integration and it is a process model that describes the characteristics of effective processes. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "The processes that an organization follows for the development of software are very important. A lot of the general performance of the company is going to be determined by the effectiveness of the processes it undertakes.</br> </br>  Companies apply CMMI principles in the planning and execution of their processes, as a collection of best practices that will improve the effectiveness of their activities, identify and achieve measurable business goals, and build better products. </br></br>  An organization can be categorized into different  <span class=\"strong\">maturity levels</span>. These levels are achieved once the organization is able to fulfill a set of  <span class=\"strong\">process areas</span>. Process areas describe the aspects of product development that need to be covered by the organization, and they are meant to adapt to the behavior of the company. Let's take a look at some process areas in the maturity levels: </br></br> <span class=\"italic\">Maturity Level 1: Initial</span></br></br>  This level is for organizations that do not have any maturity level. </br> </br>    <span class=\"italic\">Maturity Level 2: Managed</span></br></br>  <span class=\"bullet\">Measurement and Analysis</span> </br> <span class=\"bullet\">Project Monitoring and Control</span> </br> <span class=\"bullet\">Project planning</span> </br> <span class=\"bullet\">Requirements Management</span> </br> <span class=\"bullet\">Etc.</span>  </br></br>  <span class=\"italic\">Maturity Level 3: Defined</span></br></br>  <span class=\"bullet\">Decision Analysis and Resolution</span> </br> <span class=\"bullet\">Integrated Project Management</span> </br> <span class=\"bullet\">Requirements Development</span> </br> <span class=\"bullet\">Risk Management</span><br> <span class=\"bullet\">Etc.</br></br> <span class=\"italic\">Maturity Level 4: Quantitatively Managed</span></br></br>  <span class=\"bullet\">Organizational Process Performance</span></br> <span class=\"bullet\">Organizational Project Management</span></br></br>   <span class=\"italic\">Maturity Level 5: Optimizing</span></br></br>  <span class=\"bullet\">Causal Analysis and Resolution</span></br> <span class=\"bullet\">Organizational Performance Management</span>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "streamline"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to change something for making it more efficient "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Therefore, we had to streamline the process of defect tracking so that the collected data was relevant for the team. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n8le01ob04aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "jeopardize   "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to hazard, to endanger"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This helped the team collect the defect tracking data without jeopardizing the CMMI level. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n8le01ob04aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "counterproductive "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " something that is not productive or efficient"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We realized that we were carrying out the defect tracking process in a counterproductive way."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n8le01ob04aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "reluctant  "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something that is done unwillingly "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Although we were reluctant at the beginning, since we thought that any change could have affected our CMMI level 4, we decided to evaluate the company's processes performance to get an overview of the project. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n8le01ob04aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "flow diagram  "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a diagram that shows the dynamic relationships of a system "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: To do so, we built a flow diagram of the processes the team was carrying out. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n8le01ob04aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "come up with   "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to think of an idea or solution for something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(phrasal verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We wouldn't have strengthened the effectiveness of the team if we hadn't come up with a better way of gathering data.  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n8le01ob04aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for a report when collecting data in defect tracking has been useful for a project."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a short text (200 words) explaining why it was important."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share the text with your partners."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I investigate about collecting data in defect tracking."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write about collecting data when defect tracking."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about collecting data in defect tracking."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"id": 0, "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "type": "welcome", "template_override": 1}, {"_data": [], "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n8le01ob04re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "100", "image": "enpe8n8le01ob04re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<div align=\"justify\">Collecting data for defect tracking is a pivotal process for our company, and we wouldn't have been able to fix so many defects if it weren't for this process. However, our organization was having trouble with the excessive amount of data it was dealing with. We shouldn't have thought that by entering as much data as possible, we were going to improve the defect tracking process. This process could have been less tedious, but we weren't selective with the data we collected. <br></div>"}, {"time": "33000", "image": "enpe8n8le01ob04re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<div align=\"justify\">\nAlthough we were reluctant at the beginning, since we thought that any change could have affected our CMMI level 4, we decided to evaluate the company's processes performance to get an overview of the project. To do so, we built a flow diagram of the processes the team was carrying out, but we noticed that not all of the processes that were stated by the CMMI were actually being used by the team members. <br></div>"}, {"time": "62000", "image": "enpe8n8le01ob04re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<div align=\"justify\">\nWe realized that we were carrying out the defect tracking process in a counterproductive way, as the team were entering unnecessary data; thus, they were losing time when doing so because they were not going back to analyze and use all of the gathered information. Therefore, we had to streamline the process of defect tracking so that the collected data was relevant for the team. This helped the team collect the defect tracking data without jeopardizing the CMMI level. All in all, we wouldn't have strengthened the effectiveness of the team if we hadn't come up with a better way of gathering data.  <br><br>Defect tracking allowed us to collect significant information to improve our services for better, but we wouldn't have fixed so many defects if we hadn't undergone this process. Unfortunately, we could have collected more relevant data and become more efficient in fixing defects if we had refined our defect tracking process before. </div>"}], "coverimg": "enpe8n8le01ob04re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "template_override": 1, "id": 1, "title": ""}, {"_data": [], "contents": [{"value": "01 (3).jpg", "type": "img"}, {"value": "02 (3).jpg", "type": "img"}, {"value": "03 (3).jpg", "type": "img"}], "type": "static", "template_override": 1, "id": 2, "title": ""}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about the importance of collecting data when defect tracking. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can recall experiences that show the importance of collecting data when defect tracking. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can discuss the positive outcomes of refining the process of collecting data."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "How do you think that collecting data might help a project to succeed?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What do you think is the most important kind of data you need to collect when tracking defects?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "We need to know how to track defects."}], "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "id": 0, "template_override": 1}, {"stimuli_ids": [1], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " There are some <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">misconceptions</span> about defect tracking"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Content"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Listening"}], "type": "learning_skills"}, {"type": "tips", "content": [{"tip_id": 0, "type": "text", "content": "We use the word \u201c<span class=\"italic\">misconception</span>\u201d when we want to talk about a mistaken idea about something. "}]}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: Click on the play button to listen to the audio."}], "type": "post_instructions"}], "questions": [{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "type": "question"}], "responses": [{"_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "selected": 0, "correct": 0, "id": 0}, {"_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "selected": 0, "correct": 1, "id": 1}], "id": 0}], "type": "STI", "template_override": 1, "id": 1}, {"stimuli_ids": [], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "This could have been so different."}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Activity 1"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}], "type": "learning_skills"}, {"contents": [{"type": "grid_x", "content": 15}, {"type": "grid_y", "content": 15}], "type": "options"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: Find the words in the wordsearch below. Click the first letter and the last letter of the word to select it."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 attempts to submit your answers."}], "type": "post_instructions"}], "questions": [{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Some bad decisions made by a CEO could have _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ the entire project maturity level.  "}], "type": "question"}, {"type": "objective", "content": "secondary_1"}], "responses": [{"_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "selected": 0, "correct": 0, "id": 0}, {"_data": [{"type": "text", "content": "jeopardized"}, {"type": "position_x", "content": 1}, {"type": "position_y", "content": 0}, {"type": "direc